ID   2.3.1.303
DE   alpha-L-Rha-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Gal-
DE   PP-Und 2(IV)-O-acetyltransferase.
CA   alpha-L-Rha-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Gal-
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + acetyl-CoA = alpha-L-
CA   2OAcRha-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->2)-alpha-D-Man-(1->3)-alpha-D-Gal-
CA   di-trans,octa-cis-undecaprenyl diphosphate + CoA.
CC   -!- The enzyme, present in Salmonella strains that belong to group C2,
CC       participates in the biosynthesis of the repeat unit of O antigens
CC       produced by these strains.
//
ID   7.6.2.16
DE   ABC-type putrescine transporter.
AN   putrescine ABC transporter.
AN   putrescine transporting ATPase.
CA   putrescine(out) + ATP + H2O = putrescine(in) + ADP + phosphate + H(+).
CC   -!- ATP-binding cassette (ABC) type transporter, characterized by the
CC       presence of two similar ATP-binding domains/proteins and two integral
CC       membrane domains/proteins.
CC   -!- The enzyme from the bacterium Escherichia coli interacts with an
CC       extracytoplasmic substrate binding protein and mediates the high
CC       affinity uptake of putrescine.
CC   -!- Differs in specificity from EC 7.6.2.11, ABC-type polyamine
CC       transporter.
DR   Q9H7F0, AT133_HUMAN;  Q95JN5, AT133_MACFA;  Q5XF89, AT133_MOUSE;
DR   P31134, POTG_ECOLI ;
